[h1]Station Architect[/h1]

Tell the build menu what your station should produce or build: this extension works out every module needed and places them as one compact block. Nothing is bought until you press [b]Confirm[/b].

[h2][b]Features[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Target planner[/b]: say what the station should make (a ware, or ships to build or repair), not which modules; several targets in one plan.
[*] [b]Compact layout[/b]: production, storage and habitats packed tight on connection modules; build modules on the sides with clear approach lanes; docks and piers outward.
[*] [b]Full cycle and workforce[/b]: optionally every intermediate ware down to raw resources and energy, habitats for the workforce, and its food and medicine.
[*] [b]Read from the game[/b]: production rates, sunlight and workforce bonuses, module sizes, docking bays and ship build times; docks sized for the planned traffic.
[*] [b]Preview first[/b]: modules, each ware's balance per hour, workforce and warnings before anything is placed.
[*] [b]Existing stations[/b]: reads what a station makes and fills any shortfall.
[*] [b]From the map[/b]: right-click empty space, [b]Plan a station here[/b], and the build menu opens with the run started.
[*] [b]Bill route[/b]: a manual list of modules and counts, placed the same way.
[*] [b]Plot licence[/b]: shows the plot size and price where the plot costs money; [b]Optimize plot[/b] shrinks it afterwards.
[*] [b]The plan stays yours[/b]: edit, save or load it by hand; [b]Confirm module changes[/b] pays as usual, [b]Cancel module changes[/b] discards it.
[/list]
[h2][b]Limitations[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Works only inside the open build menu of a station you own, with your own blueprints.
[*] This mod requires [b]Protected UI Mode[/b] in the game's Extensions settings to be disabled.
[*] Windows version of the game only: the placement route reads the game's own editor in memory, which the native Linux build does not expose the same way. The Windows game running on Linux through Proton or Wine should work.
[*] Verified on the 8.00 and 9.00 builds of the game. On a build it does not recognise, the panel says the editor is not reachable and Run stays off; nothing else in the build menu changes.
[*] The plot is limited to the game's 20 km: a layout that needs more is refused before anything is placed.
[*] Ship build times assume the station has its build drones; a shipyard without them builds several times slower than planned.
[*] A module that fits nowhere is reported as failed, never silently dropped.
[/list]
